#EXTINF:1371 group-title="James Frazer",The Golden Bough The Magic Art And The Evolution Of Kings Volume 2 — James Frazer · XXI-DIANUS AND DIANA. Recapitulation : Rise of sacred kings endowed with magical or divine powers- The King of the Wood at Nemi seems to have personified Jupiter the god of the oak and to have mated with Diana the goddess of the oak- Dianus (Janus) and Diana originally dialectically different forms of Jupiter and Juno- Janus (Dianus) not originally a god of doors- Double-headed figure of Janus (Dianus) derived from a custom of placing him as sentinel at doorways- Parallel custom among the negroes of Surinam- Originally the King of the Wood at Nemi represented Dianus (Janus)- a duplicate form of Jupiter- the god of the oak- the thunder- and the sky. - Read by Leon Harvey - Duration 00:22:51
